course: dictionary
lesson: 12715
title: The dorsal fin
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dorsal means on or to do with the back of an animal, or the upper side of something. Scientists use it to point to a part of a body exactly, so everyone knows which side they mean.
explain: «The shark's dorsal fin cut through the waves.» The fin is on the top of the shark, on its back. Check by swapping in your meaning: "the shark's back fin cut through the waves" still makes sense, so dorsal means back.
explain: A dorsal fin helps a fish balance and steer, so it does a real job. «The dolphin turned quickly, using its dorsal fin to steer.» Dolphins have dorsal fins too, even though they are mammals and not fish.
fact: Dorsal means on or to do with the back of an animal, or the upper side of something.
fact: The dorsal fin is the fin on the back of a fish, shark, dolphin or whale.
fact: «The dorsal side of the fish is dark, and its belly is pale.»
fact: The opposite of dorsal is ventral, which means the belly side.
fact: Dolphins and whales are mammals, but they still have dorsal fins.
exercise: «The shark's dorsal fin cut through the waves.» Where is the dorsal fin? | Inside the mouth | On the tail | Under the belly | *On the shark's back
exercise: «The dorsal side of the fish is dark.» Which part of the fish is dark? | The belly | The tail | The fins underneath | *The back, or upper side
exercise: Which word is the opposite of dorsal? | *Ventral | Luminous | Curt | Dorsal
test:
«A dolphin used its dorsal fin to steer.» What does dorsal mean here? | Under the belly | *On or to do with the back | Very big | Hidden under the sand
What is a dorsal fin? | *The fin on the back of a fish or whale | The fin on the front of a bird | The tail at the end of a fish | A fin that lives in the sea floor
exam: «Dorsal» and «ventral» are opposites: which word means the belly side? | Fin | Dorsal | *Ventral | Back
